2
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:31,500
また悪い夢を見た。
Another bad dream.

3
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:38,800
陰惨な現場が日常の探偵という職業には、悪夢は付き物と言ってもいいでしょう。
Perhaps nightmares are the penalty a detective pays for being in a gruesome business.

4
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:43,000
だが、気にしている場合ではない。
So be it. She's not about to stop.

5
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:49,000
彼女のもとに、また新たな事件が舞い込んでできているからだ。
Not when there are new cases to be solved.

6
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,100
(Unhappy?) 悩める人の子よ
(Unhappy?) Oh, troubled child of man,

7
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,600
(Unlucky?) 人成らざる者も
(Unlucky?) and those who aren't human either,

8
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,100
(Be happy!) 弛まず目指せよ
(Be happy!) strive without faltering.

9
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:04,000
(Undead) 生きているんだし
(Undead) After all, you are alive.

10
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,500
目を逸らした過去も
The past you averted your eyes from,

11
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,100
退屈な未来も
and the boring future too,

12
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,800
カウンセリング やれやれ
are still counseling you... Good grief.

13
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,500
古今東西 ピースピース
East and west, past and present, peace, peace!

14
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,300
(Unhappy?)

15
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:13,800
(Unlucky?)

16
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,300
(Be happy!)

17
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:17,300
(Undead)

18
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:26,500
ねえねえ ねえねえ 何だか どうして
Hey, hey, somehow, why is it

19
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:29,000
戦っているような そんな気がするの
that I feel like I'm fighting a battle?

20
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,500
触れられない 触れたくもない
Untouchable, don't even want to touch:

21
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:32,100
過去の自分 自分 自分 自分 と
with the past me, me, me, me...

22
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,800
もうとっくに死んでる 透明な亡霊と対決
Showdown with a transparent ghost long since dead.

23
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,300
幼気で痛い記憶の奥
In the depths of childish, painful memories,

24
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:38,800
残念? もう居ないのに
Sad? Even though it's no longer there...

25
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,400
あれ? そっちが良い? アイロニーね
Huh? You prefer that side? How ironic.

26
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:44,200
透かされているのは現在の自分?
Is the one being seen through the present me?

27
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,800
ナンセンス 消えないレッテル
Nonsense, a label that won't go away.

28
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,300
Yes! 要は コンプレックス
Yes! In short, a complex.

29
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:49,000
取り憑かれているみたい
It's like being possessed.

30
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,900
巻き付いたまま まだ 離れない
Coiled around, still not letting go.

31
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,600
在りし日の自分
The self from days gone by...

32
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,200
Undead 死んじゃいない
Undead, not dead yet!

33
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,800
お前とお前の連鎖
A chain of you and yourself.

34
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:00,100
生きていることとは 変わり続けることだ
To be alive means to keep changing!

35
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:01,800
不幸に甘んじて
Don't settle for unhappiness

36
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,400
満足するなよ
and be content with it!

37
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:07,000
幸せになろうとしないなんて 卑怯だ
Not even trying to be happy is cowardly.

38
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,800
この世 この世は 奇怪 奇怪 ファンタジー
This world, this world is a bizarre fantasy.

39
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,800
次は鬼が出るか 蛇が出るか
What will come out next, a demon or a snake?

40
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:17,000
出会って 遭って やっと 始まる 物語
Meeting, encountering, a story finally begins!

41
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,800
さあ人か 化物か
Now, is it human or monster?

42
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:22,000
閑話休題 ピースピース
Back to business, peace, peace!

43
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,500
Past & future

44
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,000
Can't change the past

45
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,500
Past & future

46
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,000
Run for the future

47
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,500
カ・カ・カットイン
C-C-Cut in!

48
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:33,200
何だか どうして 未来になんぞ
Somehow, why is it that in the future

49
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:37,300
何の希望もない 期待出来ないような気がして
I feel like there's no hope, nothing to expect?

50
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:40,400
もう随分生きてる 既視感とテンプレで食傷
Lived long enough, sick of déjà vu and cliches.

51
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:43,000
素敵な出来事の気配もない
Not even a sign of anything wonderful happening.

52
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,400
残念 積んだ経験の因果
Too bad, the karma of accumulated experience:

53
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:47,500
形骸化された神話と退屈な進化
hollowed-out myths and boring evolution.

54
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,000
要は 刺激が欲しいんだ
In short, I just want excitement!

55
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,500
飽きちゃった 慣れちゃった
Got sick of it, got used to it.

56
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,200
なんて 整っていくガイダンス
Such is the guidance taking shape,

57
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,900
増えるコンプライアンス
increasing compliance,

58
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,600
蓋されていくみたい
like being put under a lid.

59
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,200
吸い尽くして
Sucking it all dry...

60
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:00,800
あれも これも どれも 同じ味がする
That one, this one, whichever, all taste the same.

61
00:05:00,148 --> 00:05:03,048
あー 同じ アンチが ぐるぐる
Ah, the same haters going 'round and 'round...

62
00:05:03,048 --> 00:05:04,248
UNDEAD!

63
00:05:04,248 --> 00:05:07,548
信じない脳内 脳内の連鎖
Unbelieving mind, a chain reaction in my head,

64
00:05:07,548 --> 00:05:10,848
一卵性も過去も未来も今にあるんだ
Identical twins, the past, the future—it's all right here in the present.

65
00:05:10,848 --> 00:05:14,248
生きていくだけ愚直に果たせよ
Fulfill your life with foolish honesty!

66
00:05:14,248 --> 00:05:16,348
目指せハッピーエンド
Aim for a happy ending!

67
00:05:16,348 --> 00:05:17,348
UNDEAD!

68
00:05:17,348 --> 00:05:19,848
信じない脳内 生きているんだ
Unbelieving mind, I am alive!

69
00:05:19,848 --> 00:05:23,748
幸せを諦めてしまうな 独り言
Don't give up on happiness—just a monologue.

70
00:05:23,748 --> 00:05:27,548
ただ苦しみになれてさえ耐えているだけじゃ
If you just endure and grow accustomed to the pain,

71
00:05:27,548 --> 00:05:30,248
死んでいるも同然 屍
You're no better than dead—a corpse.

72
00:05:30,248 --> 00:05:31,048
UNDEAD!

73
00:05:31,048 --> 00:05:33,048
悩める人の世
In this troubled world of men,

74
00:05:33,048 --> 00:05:36,548
人ならざるものも 開幕目指すよ
Even those non-humans aim for the opening curtain!

75
00:05:36,548 --> 00:05:38,848
生きているんだろう 命減ったって
Aren't you alive? Even if life diminishes,

76
00:05:38,848 --> 00:05:41,248
幸せになるのも どうせ未定の未来なら
Becoming happy is an undecided future anyway.

77
00:05:41,248 --> 00:05:43,548
お前だ ここで起死回生
It's up to you—turn the tables right here!

78
00:05:43,548 --> 00:05:46,048
一切合切 死なない証 ピースピース
Everything, proof of being undead—peace peace!

79
00:05:46,048 --> 00:05:48,848
Past and future, can't change the past

80
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:52,548
Past and future, run for the future

81
00:05:52,548 --> 00:05:55,548
人となあるとトコトン やっとめぐった
Living as a person, we finally met.

82
00:05:55,548 --> 00:05:58,848
生きて行こうか 負けも知ら...
Shall we live on? Without knowing defeat...

83
00:06:28,848 --> 00:06:36,048
ダメダメダメ 脳味噌の中からやめろ馬鹿と叫ぶモラリティ
No, no, no—from inside my brain, morality screams, "Stop it, you idiot!"

84
00:06:36,048 --> 00:06:43,248
ダーリンメミーダーリン 半端なくラブ ときめき破滅的フィロソフィー
Darling, baby darling—an outrageous kind of love, a throbbing, destructive philosophy.

85
00:06:43,248 --> 00:06:46,048
死ぬほど可愛い 上目遣い
A deadly cute, upward glance,

86
00:06:46,048 --> 00:06:48,048
何かしらの法に触れるくらい
That probably breaks some kind of law.

87
00:06:48,048 --> 00:06:50,048
散らまく乱心 気づけば投身
Spreading madness everywhere, before I know it, I jump right in.

88
00:06:50,048 --> 00:06:53,048
この世に生まれた君が悪い
It's your fault for being born into this world.

89
00:06:53,048 --> 00:06:57,248
やたらとしんどい 恋の患い バラバラになる頭とこの身体
This lovesickness is ridiculously painful, my head and body falling apart.

90
00:06:57,248 --> 00:07:04,548
頸動脈から愛してるが噴き出て アイリスアウト
"I love you" bursts out from my carotid artery—IRIS OUT.

91
00:07:04,548 --> 00:07:08,048
一体全体どうしようこの思いはどうしよう
What on earth am I supposed to do with these feelings?

92
00:07:08,048 --> 00:07:11,848
肋骨の奥をどうしよう 砂糖の芯が溶けてゲロになりそう
What do I do with what's deep inside my ribs? The sugary core melts, turning into vomit.

93
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:15,548
瞳孔バチ開いて溺れ死にそう
My pupils blown wide open, feels like I'm drowning to death.

94
00:07:15,548 --> 00:07:19,048
今この世で君だけが大正解
Right now in this world, only you are the correct answer.

95
00:07:19,048 --> 00:07:26,048
ダーリン ダーリン ダーリン ダーリン
Darling, darling, darling, darling...

96
00:07:26,048 --> 00:07:30,048
ひっくり返っても逆立ちしても勝ち目なんかない
Even if everything turned upside down, I'd have no chance of winning.

97
00:07:30,048 --> 00:07:33,248
君だけがルール外 奴等もれなく黒しかない角取り兄弟
Only you are outside the rules, while everyone else is nothing but black tiles on a board.

98
00:07:33,248 --> 00:07:37,048
君が笑顔で放ったアバダケダブラで額に傷痕残ったまま申し訳ねえな
The Avada Kedavra you cast with a smile leaves a scar on my forehead, sorry about that.

99
00:07:37,048 --> 00:07:40,048
矢を挿して 貫いて ここ急所点
Shoot the arrow, pierce right through—here's my weak spot.

100
00:07:40,048 --> 00:07:43,048
死ぬほど可愛い 上目遣い
A deadly cute, upward glance,

101
00:07:43,048 --> 00:07:44,848
何かしらの法に触れるくらい
That probably breaks some kind of law.

102
00:07:44,848 --> 00:07:47,048
散らまく乱心 気づけば投身
Spreading madness everywhere, before I know it, I jump right in.

103
00:07:47,048 --> 00:07:49,048
この世に生まれた君が悪い
It's your fault for being born into this world.

104
00:07:49,048 --> 00:07:51,048
偽物でもいい 何でもいい
Fake or not, it doesn't matter, anything is fine.

105
00:07:51,048 --> 00:07:53,048
今君と名付いてる全てが欲しい
Right now I want everything that bears your name.

106
00:07:53,048 --> 00:07:55,548
頸動脈から愛してるが噴き出て
"I love you" bursts out from my carotid artery—

107
00:07:55,548 --> 00:07:59,048
アイリスアウト
IRIS OUT.

108
00:08:00,048 --> 00:08:02,548
アイリスアウト
IRIS OUT.

109
00:08:06,048 --> 00:08:08,548
アイリスアウト
IRIS OUT.

110
00:08:08,548 --> 00:08:12,048
一体全体どうしようこの思いはどうしよう
What on earth am I supposed to do with these feelings?

111
00:08:12,048 --> 00:08:15,548
肋骨の奥をどうしよう 砂糖の芯が溶けてゲロになりそう
What do I do with what's deep inside my ribs? The sugary core melts, turning into vomit.

112
00:08:15,548 --> 00:08:19,048
瞳孔バチ開いて溺れ死にそう
My pupils blown wide open, feels like I'm drowning to death.

113
00:08:19,048 --> 00:08:23,048
今この世で君だけが大正解
Right now in this world, only you are the correct answer.

114
00:08:23,048 --> 00:08:30,048
ダーリン ダーリン ダーリン ダーリン
Darling, darling, darling, darling...

115
00:08:30,048 --> 00:08:37,048
アイリスアウト
IRIS OUT.

116
00:08:45,048 --> 00:08:49,848
ある殺人事件を調べてほしいという匿名の依頼。
An anonymous request asking to investigate a murder case.

117
00:08:50,048 --> 00:08:57,248
手紙に被害者の情報はほとんどなく、ましてや犯人の情報は皆無であった。
The letter contained almost no information on the victim, and none on the culprit.

118
00:08:57,848 --> 00:09:05,048
あまりに不可解な謎の手紙。イタズラの可能性もある。けど…
An overly cryptic, mysterious letter. It could be a prank, but...

119
00:09:05,548 --> 00:09:06,848
おや？
Oh?

120
00:09:08,848 --> 00:09:12,548
おはよう、アーニャ！依頼された絵が完成しましたよ～。
Good morning, Anya! I finished your commissioned drawing~

121
00:09:12,548 --> 00:09:17,048
一伊那爾栖（にのまえ いなにす）。この町一番の肖像画家だ。
Ninomae Ina'nis. The top portrait painter in this town.

122
00:09:17,548 --> 00:09:21,048
あの…私の顔に何かついてます？
Um... is there something on my face?

123
00:09:21,048 --> 00:09:28,848
事件の手がかりがない以上、解決の糸口を見つけるには彼女の才能を頼る必要があった。
With no clues to the case, I needed her talent to find a breakthrough.

124
00:09:29,048 --> 00:09:30,848
アーニャ？
Anya?

125
00:09:31,048 --> 00:09:37,048
とはいえこういった事件では、誰もが容疑者になりうる。
However, in a case like this, anyone could be a suspect.

126
00:09:37,048 --> 00:09:42,848
そう、この純粋で可憐なイナでさえ―
Yes, even this pure and lovely Ina—

127
00:09:43,048 --> 00:09:44,248
わぁぁーっ！
WAH!

128
00:09:44,248 --> 00:09:45,548
うわっ！
Whoa!

129
00:09:45,848 --> 00:09:49,848
ごめんなさい。じーっと見られてたからつい…。どうかしましたか？
Sorry! You were staring so intently... Is something wrong?

130
00:09:50,048 --> 00:09:52,548
いや別に…それっぽい雰囲気を出そうとしてただけ。
No, not really... I was just trying to create a detective vibe.

131
00:09:52,848 --> 00:09:56,048
それより、頼んでた絵はできた？
More importantly, is the drawing I asked for finished?

132
00:09:56,048 --> 00:09:57,248
できました〜！
Yes, it is~!

133
00:09:57,548 --> 00:10:00,048
描きましたけど、それ誰なんですか？
I drew it, but who is that anyway?

134
00:10:00,123 --> 00:10:01,423
Who's this a picture of anyway?

135
00:10:01,523 --> 00:10:03,523
The victim from a case I'm working.

136
00:10:03,823 --> 00:10:06,623
Anyway, you're charging the standard fee, right?

137
00:10:06,823 --> 00:10:10,523
Sorry, but can you put it on my tab?

138
00:10:10,823 --> 00:10:14,523
But you put the last one on your tab too...

139
00:10:15,023 --> 00:10:20,023
Maybe we could do a trade then? I'll solve one case for you for free.

140
00:10:20,523 --> 00:10:24,523
Oooorrr... I'll trade you for a song~
Or... I'll trade you for a song.

141
00:10:24,623 --> 00:10:25,523
Huh?

142
00:10:25,623 --> 00:10:27,823
Come on! You've been so serious lately.

143
00:10:28,023 --> 00:10:29,823
You gotta get loose sometimes.
You gotta unwind sometimes.

144
00:10:30,023 --> 00:10:34,523
So one song with me, and you get to keep the picture. That's the deal~

145
00:10:34,823 --> 00:10:37,023
If that's what you want, then alright!

146
00:10:47,523 --> 00:10:51,823
大きな白いキャンバスに 虚構のコラージュを貼るよ
On a big white canvas, I'll paste a collage of fiction.

147
00:10:52,023 --> 00:10:56,523
どこからんでも綺麗に映る 誇張された天使がいたよ
An exaggerated angel that looks beautiful from anywhere was there.

148
00:11:08,523 --> 00:11:13,523
まだ人と言うには新しくなくても見えた 起きるため立ち寄った美術展のセザンヌに
Even if not new enough to be called a person, I saw it in Cézanne at the art exhibition I stopped by to wake up.

149
00:11:19,023 --> 00:11:23,523
何も分かんないままただ知らずに見ても勝てた 赤 ずっと塗り込んだばっか 嫉妬すぐだった
Even looking without understanding, I won. Just layered on red, jealousy followed quickly.

150
00:11:29,023 --> 00:11:34,023
気取り筆の画家だけどそこがいいな
A painter with a pretentious brush, but I like that about them.

151
00:11:34,523 --> 00:11:39,023
くだらない異彩だなそのまま
Such a meaningless, unique color, just as it is.

152
00:11:39,523 --> 00:11:44,023
切って貼った皮 抱いてみえた嘘
Skin cut and pasted, a lie seen while embracing.

153
00:11:44,523 --> 00:11:49,023
笑うように浮いたあまら
Surplus floating as if laughing.

154
