00:23:33,246 --> 00:23:36,546
僕が 覚醒 逆転 ey
My awakening, reversal, ey

328
00:23:57,846 --> 00:24:01,546
以上がこちらで調べた情報です。いかがですか？
So that's everything I've got so far. What do you think?

329
00:24:02,046 --> 00:24:16,846
ここは大空警察。数々の難事件を解決してきた優秀な警察から今回の事件に関するさらなる情報を得るべく、探偵は警察署を訪れていた。
And so, here she visits the Oozora Police. With their stellar track of solving mysterious cases like this one easily, she hopes that they can give her some leads.

330
00:24:17,246 --> 00:24:26,046
ばっからー！事件の捜査は我々プロに任せておけばいいんだよ！
I think you should leave the investigating to the professionals.

331
00:24:26,546 --> 00:24:31,546
何？被害者の服に魔力の痕跡があったって？
I mean, magical residue on the victim's clothing?

332
00:24:32,046 --> 00:24:35,046
そうだ！そんなバカな話があるか！
Yes! That is very silly!

333
00:24:35,246 --> 00:24:42,546
こいつ、次、自分自身が凶器かもしれないとか言い出すんじゃないですか、署長！
Next, she's going to tell me that SHE's actually involved and might be the murder weapon.

334
00:24:53,046 --> 00:24:54,246
それだ！
Wait, that's it!

335
00:24:54,246 --> 00:24:55,246
はぁ？
Huh?

336
00:24:55,546 --> 00:25:00,046
こいつ今、自分が凶器だって自白した？
Did she just confess to being the murder weapon?

337
00:25:00,094 --> 00:25:01,094
よく分かんないっす
I'm not really sure.

338
00:25:01,094 --> 00:25:03,594
ボクが言ったのはただの冗談で...
What I said was just a joke...

339
00:25:03,894 --> 00:25:08,994
もしかしてボク、無意識のうちに真実をつかんでいたのか！？
Could it be that I subconsciously knew the truth all along?!

340
00:25:09,194 --> 00:25:10,994
お前天才か！？
Are you a genius?!

341
00:25:11,094 --> 00:25:14,294
おや、これはいよいよ事件解決...
Oh my, could this mean the case...

342
00:25:14,294 --> 00:25:16,594
になってしまうのか？
...is finally solved?

343
00:25:16,594 --> 00:25:18,594
事件解決しちゃった！
I solved the case!

344
00:25:19,394 --> 00:25:23,594
違う違う。私は凶器じゃないですよ。
No, no. I'm not the murder weapon.

345
00:25:23,794 --> 00:25:27,094
異議あり！さっき自白しただろ！
OBJECTION! You already confessed just now!

346
00:25:27,194 --> 00:25:33,794
私が言いたいのは、この事件にはまた別の古代兵器が関わっているかもしれないということ。
What I mean is, another ancient weapon might be involved in this case.

347
00:25:33,894 --> 00:25:36,194
だから布に魔力が残っていたんだ。
That's why there was magical residue on the cloth.

348
00:25:37,094 --> 00:25:40,594
なんだ、そういうことか...
Oh, so that's what it was...

349
00:25:41,094 --> 00:25:44,994
僕が事件を解決できたと思ったのに...
And here I thought I had solved the case...

350
00:25:45,094 --> 00:25:47,094
まあ次がんばれよ。
Well, try harder next time.

351
00:25:47,194 --> 00:25:53,694
でもなぁ、現場の近くで変なものを見たっていう報告も届いてるんだ。
But you know, we've received reports of people seeing weird things near the scene.

352
00:25:53,794 --> 00:26:04,994
その魔力の痕跡とやらが超常的な力によるものだって言うなら... 変な幻覚が見えた人がいるのもそいつの影響ってこと？
If that magical residue is caused by supernatural powers, does that mean the weird hallucinations people saw were also its doing?

353
00:26:05,194 --> 00:26:10,094
それはまだ分かりませんが、謎は必ず解いてみせましょう。
We don't know that yet, but I will definitely solve this mystery.

354
00:26:10,194 --> 00:26:12,994
じゃあうちの捜査資料を持って行っていいよ。
Then you can take our investigation files with you.

355
00:26:13,094 --> 00:26:15,594
民間人にあげちゃダメっすよ！
You can't give them to a civilian!

356
00:26:15,694 --> 00:26:18,994
でもこいつさぁ、なんか天才の匂いしね？
But doesn't she kind of seem like a genius?

357
00:26:19,094 --> 00:26:23,094
さっきはボクのこと天才って言ったじゃないですかぁ...
You just called me a genius a moment ago...

358
00:26:23,194 --> 00:26:24,994
どんな情報でも助かりますよ。
Any information would be helpful.

359
00:26:25,094 --> 00:26:32,894
ただし！資料が欲しいなら、タダというわけにはいかんな！
However! If you want the files, it won't come for free!

360
00:26:33,094 --> 00:26:37,094
これ、また歌う流れですか？
Is this turning into another singing segment?

361
00:26:43,594 --> 00:26:47,294
それは知らない 何も知らない
I don't know that, I know nothing.

362
00:26:47,294 --> 00:26:50,894
何も見てない 誰も見てない
I haven't seen anything, nobody has seen anything.

363
00:26:50,894 --> 00:26:54,694
空を見ての 見えない夜の
Looking up at the sky, on a night where you can't see,

364
00:26:54,694 --> 00:26:57,994
欠けた月に 密かに
secretly under the crescent moon.

365
00:26:58,094 --> 00:27:01,894
これはなんだ それは何か
What is this? What is that?

366
00:27:01,894 --> 00:27:05,394
ここは試し それで宜しい
This is a trial, is that fine?

367
00:27:05,494 --> 00:27:08,994
走る逃げる 逃がす探す
Running, escaping, letting escape, searching,

368
00:27:08,994 --> 00:27:12,594
好きな欠けた 場所へ
to a favorite broken place.

369
00:27:12,694 --> 00:27:25,094
アララ...
Ah-ra-ra...

370
00:27:26,094 --> 00:27:29,694
もうさ 咎められなく
That's right, without being blamed,

371
00:27:29,694 --> 00:27:33,294
そうさ 咎められなく
yeah, without being blamed,

372
00:27:33,294 --> 00:27:36,794
衝動 収まらず
an uncontained impulse,

373
00:27:36,794 --> 00:27:40,394
なぜか なぜか 知らん
for some reason, I don't know why.

374
00:27:40,494 --> 00:27:44,294
最悪だ 厚重の靴を履いて 脱いで踊れ
It's the worst! Put on heavy shoes, take them off and dance!

375
00:27:44,294 --> 00:27:47,894
最低感 なんでなんでっつって なんか何かと重なって
The worst feeling! Asking why, why, overlapping with something or other.

376
00:27:47,894 --> 00:27:51,894
最悪だ どうもこうもしねえよ 勝手にしやがれ
It's the worst! Nothing can be done, do whatever you want!

377
00:27:51,894 --> 00:27:55,394
最低感 いやもう本当 最悪だーだーだーだーだー
The worst feeling! No really, it's the absolute worst!

378
00:27:55,494 --> 00:28:02,394
誰のせい？ 誰のせい？ 憑き纏う 見える意識の裏側に
Whose fault? Whose fault? Hauntingly clinging to the reverse side of conscious mind,

379
00:28:02,494 --> 00:28:08,894
大きく開いた黒い穴 分かる 分かる 分かる
a big open black hole. I understand, I understand, I understand.

380
00:28:09,094 --> 00:28:12,394
許す 許せん 許す 許せん
Forgive, unforgivable, forgive, unforgivable.

381
00:28:12,494 --> 00:28:16,094
可愛い えへへ 怖い
Cute, ehehe, scary.

382
00:28:16,094 --> 00:28:17,394
りんご
Apple,

383
00:28:17,394 --> 00:28:18,594
ゴリラ
gorilla,

384
00:28:18,594 --> 00:28:19,594
落語
rakugo,

385
00:28:19,594 --> 00:28:20,594
こちら
this way,

386
00:28:20,594 --> 00:28:21,594
ラクダ
camel,

387
00:28:21,594 --> 00:28:22,294
ダブル
double,

388
00:28:22,294 --> 00:28:23,094
ラマダン
Ramadan!

389
00:28:37,894 --> 00:28:44,794
私達 絶対に見てません 聞いてません 知ったこっちゃありません
We definitely didn't see anything, didn't hear anything, it's none of our business!

390
00:28:44,894 --> 00:28:53,694
光を疾走 影に一突き 許されざる思考を 当てはまらない情を 綴って生きていこうじゃありませんか
Sprinting through the light, a thrust in the shadows, shall we live on spelling out unpardonable thoughts and unfitting emotions?

391
00:28:53,794 --> 00:28:57,294
鼓動 狂おしく
Wild heartbeat,

392
00:29:00,094 --> 00:29:00,894
狂躁 意味もなく
meaningless frenzy,

393
00:29:00,894 --> 00:29:04,394
エゴ 自己満足
ego and self-satisfaction.

394
00:29:04,494 --> 00:29:08,594
だから...
So...

395
00:29:08,694 --> 00:29:12,694
最高だ 脳が硬化してんだ ぶっ壊して叫べ
It's the best! The brain is hardening, smash it and scream!

396
00:29:12,694 --> 00:29:16,594
最高感 なんでなんでっつって まこまこはねちゃって
The best feeling! Asking why, why, Mako-Mako is bouncing!

397
00:29:16,694 --> 00:29:20,194
最高だ 好奇心で結構 勝手に生きたれ
It's the best! Curiosity is fine, live as you please!

398
00:29:20,294 --> 00:29:24,094
最高感 いやもう本当 最高だーだーだーだーだー
The best feeling! No really, it's the absolute best!

399
00:29:24,194 --> 00:29:30,894
昔 昔の思い出つき 無意義 無意義の人ばかり
Old, old memories attached, full of meaningless, meaningless people.

400
00:29:30,994 --> 00:29:37,094
無邪気 無敵の生まれつき それが それが
Innocent and invincible by nature, that's it, that's it.

401
00:29:37,294 --> 00:29:45,394
責任集合体 あんたもわたしも関係ない
Collective body of responsibility, you and I have nothing to do with it!

402
00:29:45,494 --> 00:29:53,094
責任集合体 楽しくやってりゃもう満開
Collective body of responsibility, as long as we're having fun, we're in full bloom!

403
00:29:53,194 --> 00:29:59,894
勝手にやってりゃ問題なし それは知らない 何も知らない 何も言わない 何も...
If we do as we like, there's no problem! I don't know that, I know nothing, I say nothing, nothing...

404
00:30:00,269 --> 00:30:01,169
ない
No

405
00:30:01,169 --> 00:30:02,069
ちょっと
Wait a sec

406
00:30:02,069 --> 00:30:03,069
違い
No, that's wrong

407
00:30:03,069 --> 00:30:04,169
夢の話
A story about dreams...

408
00:30:04,169 --> 00:30:05,669
そういうカットで
Cut it like that.

409
00:30:05,669 --> 00:30:07,569
それじゃ
Well then...

410
00:30:16,269 --> 00:30:20,369
超常的な力が殺人事件に関わっている？
A supernatural occurrence, happening in a murder case?

411
00:30:20,869 --> 00:30:24,069
いやいやそんな、ねぇ？
That's just unbelievable, right?

412
00:30:24,869 --> 00:30:30,869
にわかには信じがたいが、今の手がかりから推理するとそういうことになる。
She had a hard time believing it, but all the hints said otherwise.

413
00:30:31,569 --> 00:30:37,269
まだパズルのピースがピタリとはまらないこの不思議で奇妙な事件。
Still, there were pieces of this puzzle that refused to fit in this strange case.

414
00:30:37,869 --> 00:30:42,269
探偵は信頼できる情報源に頼ることにした。
So the detective turned to a reliable source for help.

415
00:30:44,269 --> 00:30:45,869
あっ、来てくれたー
Ah, I'm glad you came!

416
00:30:46,369 --> 00:30:48,869
...なんで君達まで？
...And why are you guys also here?

417
00:30:49,869 --> 00:30:53,069
We heard Zeta was coming over, and decided to bug ya!

418
00:30:53,269 --> 00:30:54,669
Yes, yes. I see.

419
00:30:55,269 --> 00:30:56,669
Aww, come on!

420
00:30:56,869 --> 00:30:59,569
Anyway, Zeta, did you find anything?

421
00:30:59,869 --> 00:31:03,869
Of course! I'm not an elite secret agent for nothing!

422
00:31:04,069 --> 00:31:11,269
Between the portrait from Ina and the files from the Oozora Police, I've been able to positively ID the murder victim.

423
00:31:11,269 --> 00:31:14,069
But... what I found is weird.

424
00:31:14,069 --> 00:31:15,269
How so?

425
00:31:15,569 --> 00:31:20,269
Well, when I investigated their history, I found that they actually lived centuries ago.

426
00:31:20,269 --> 00:31:25,869
So how they were also somehow murdered just days ago... it doesn't make any sense.

427
00:31:26,069 --> 00:31:29,569
Did you perhaps confuse your information? Or...

428
00:31:29,869 --> 00:31:33,869
Actually, things are finally starting to make sense.

429
00:31:34,069 --> 00:31:34,869
Oh?

430
00:31:35,069 --> 00:31:37,669
A victim caught between two times.

431
00:31:37,869 --> 00:31:40,869
One who died in two different ways.

432
00:31:41,069 --> 00:31:46,269
Not many exist who can cause time and dimensions to warp in a way to make that possible...

433
00:31:46,569 --> 00:31:49,869
...but you're one of them.

434
00:31:50,869 --> 00:31:53,069
Well done, detective.

435
00:31:53,269 --> 00:31:56,869
Took you long enough. I was this close to telling ya the whole thing.

436
00:31:57,069 --> 00:32:00,069
You helped enough with this "anonymous" letter about the murder.

437
00:32:00,069 --> 00:32:02,569
O-oh, you figured out that was me?

438
00:32:02,569 --> 00:32:04,869
I recognized your writing style.

439
00:32:05,069 --> 00:32:09,569
W-wait, I don't get it. What does Moona have to do with the victim?

440
00:32:09,869 --> 00:32:14,669
She took a murder victim from another space and time, and moved them into our dimension.

441
00:32:14,869 --> 00:32:18,869
The one you IDed was this universe's version of the same person.

442
00:32:19,069 --> 00:32:23,569
Uh... okay. But then why?

443
00:32:23,869 --> 00:32:29,869
That is an important question, but there's one I want answered even more.

444
00:32:30,569 --> 00:32:33,869
Are you... responsible for my dreams?

445
00:32:34,069 --> 00:32:35,569
No.

446
00:32:36,069 --> 00:32:40,869
After I learned about your dreams, I used my powers to search for the source of them.

447
00:32:41,069 --> 00:32:44,869
I found a spirit reaching out from time and dimensions.

448
00:32:45,069 --> 00:32:48,869
All I've done is try to help them by making the bridge a little easier...

449
00:32:49,069 --> 00:32:52,569
With my help! I mean, it was my idea...

450
00:32:53,069 --> 00:32:54,869
True.

451
00:32:55,269 --> 00:33:00,269
Though doing it this way has caused some of what you've been experiencing to leak to other people.

452
00:33:00,569 --> 00:33:04,569
We're going to have to apologize to the KFP workers...

453
00:33:04,869 --> 00:33:08,069
But why is the spirit reaching out to me of all people?

454
00:33:08,269 --> 00:33:13,569
It wouldn't be right for me to answer those questions. It's not my story to tell.

455
00:33:13,869 --> 00:33:17,869
Open yourself up to the spirits, and they'll do the rest.

456
00:33:18,069 --> 00:33:20,869
I got a way to make yourself more open to spirits!

457
00:33:21,069 --> 00:33:22,869
Is it through song?

458
00:33:23,069 --> 00:33:24,869
Huh? How'd you know?

459
00:33:25,069 --> 00:33:27,569
Lucky guess...

460
00:33:55,269 --> 00:33:59,869
思い返してた 思い出の中で泣いてた
I was looking back, crying in my memories

461
00:34:00,069 --> 00:34:05,569
負担しかない夢と孤独を抱えて笑ってた
Carrying dreams and solitude that were only burdens, I laughed

462
00:34:05,869 --> 00:34:10,869
この畳み掛く質問 堪えないゴミに言い返してしまいそうな
About to talk back to these relentless questions and unbearable nonsense

463
00:34:11,069 --> 00:34:16,069
焦りと不安がにじんで 涙に飲まれてしまう
Impatience and anxiety bleed through, swallowed up by tears

464
00:34:16,269 --> 00:34:21,869
誰一人欠けることはない ちぐはぐな
Not a single person is missing from our mismatched...

465
00:34:21,869 --> 00:34:26,569
僕らの思いが音になって繋ぐ
...feelings that turn into sound and connect us

466
00:34:26,569 --> 00:34:31,069
こだまして忘れないようかき鳴らして
Strumming so it echoes and won't be forgotten

467
00:34:31,069 --> 00:34:36,869
あの日僕らは間違っていなかったんだと知る
Knowing that we weren't wrong on that day

468
00:34:36,869 --> 00:34:42,869
伸ばして仕舞い込んだ一線の光探して
Reaching out, searching for that ray of light tucked away

469
00:34:42,869 --> 00:34:48,869
君の声を聞かせて ここにいるって叫んでくれよ
Let me hear your voice, shout out that you're here

470
00:34:49,069 --> 00:34:54,069
その手を離さないで
Don't let go of that hand

471
00:34:56,569 --> 00:35:00,069
世界に僕だけが取り残されてしまう
I'll end up left behind all alone in this world

472
00:35:00,117 --> 00:35:01,217
…んだよな
...right?

473
00:35:01,217 --> 00:35:06,717
暗闇の中で立ち止まり 手放してしまう
Standing still in the darkness, letting go.

474
00:35:06,717 --> 00:35:11,917
心が通じ合えないのなら 心殺してしまうなら
If our hearts cannot understand each other, if we must kill our feelings...

475
00:35:11,917 --> 00:35:17,117
一人でいた方が楽に生きられたのかな
Would it have been easier to live alone?

476
00:35:17,117 --> 00:35:22,517
憧れ 理想に強く惹かれる感情が
If feelings strongly drawn to longings and ideals...

477
00:35:22,517 --> 00:35:29,617
僕らを 引き寄せてしまうのなら 応えて
...pull us together, then answer me.

478
00:35:37,117 --> 00:35:44,917
誤魔化していーく まだ終わっちゃいないんだ 僕ら延長戦なんだろう
Deceiving, keeping it up... It's not over yet. We're in overtime, aren't we?

479
00:35:45,117 --> 00:35:49,617
この音が途切れるまで
Until this sound fades away...

480
00:35:49,617 --> 00:35:54,117
子供の頃に描いたヒーロー
The hero I envisioned as a child...

481
00:35:54,117 --> 00:35:58,317
君の出番が待ってる
...your turn is waiting.

482
00:35:58,317 --> 00:36:03,917
誤魔化していーく 忘れないよう鍵鳴らした意味を
Deceiving, so as not to forget the meaning of ringing the key.

483
00:36:03,917 --> 00:36:09,317
あの日僕らは間違いじゃなかったと知る
We come to know that we weren't wrong that day.

484
00:36:09,317 --> 00:36:14,917
閉ざしてしまい込んだ一線の向こう側探して
Searching for the other side of the line we locked away,

485
00:36:14,917 --> 00:36:18,317
君の声を聞かせて
Let me hear your voice.

486
00:36:18,317 --> 00:36:21,617
ここにいるって叫んでくれよ
Shout out that you're right here.

487
00:36:21,617 --> 00:36:27,617
その手を解かないで
Don't untie those hands.

488
00:36:38,617 --> 00:36:43,817
魂に心を開け？ 簡単に言ってくれる。
Opening up to the spirit? That was a tall order.

489
00:36:44,617 --> 00:36:53,417
探偵になる前の彼女の人生において、他者に心を開くのは危険な行為だった。
In her life before being a detective, opening up to someone was dangerous.

490
00:36:54,117 --> 00:36:57,117
今でもその本能は変わらない。
That instinct still lingers.

491
00:37:00,117 --> 00:37:02,917
結局何もしんてんはなかった。
This was getting her nowhere.

492
00:37:03,117 --> 00:37:09,617
謎はまだ残っているが、彼女はここのところ無理が続いていた。
She still had questions she needed answered, but maybe she had wound herself up too much.

493
00:37:13,317 --> 00:37:16,117
少し休まなければ。
She needed a break.

494
00:37:25,317 --> 00:37:29,617
Hello everyone! I'm Hatsune Miku, a virtual idol!

495
00:37:29,917 --> 00:37:34,117
Well, that's what everyone seems to think at least... Right?

496
00:37:35,117 --> 00:37:36,617
Oya oya oya oya!

497
00:37:36,617 --> 00:37:39,117
Miku-chan! Anya-chan!

498
00:37:39,117 --> 00:37:41,117
Oya oya oya oya!

499
00:37:41,117 --> 00:37:44,317
Anya-chan! 一緒に歌おう！
Anya-chan! Let's sing together!

500
00:37:44,617 --> 00:37:47,417
I wake up to a call, put my frilly outfit on now

501
00:37:47,417 --> 00:37:49,917
It’s time I open up my eyes and start the day

502
00:37:49,917 --> 00:37:52,617
I combat till the dawn until every villain’s gone

503
00:37:52,617 --> 00:37:54,917
A clumsy trip and now I’ve fallen to my butt

504
00:37:54,917 --> 00:37:57,717
With my magical phone and a silly little ringtone

505
00:37:57,717 --> 00:38:00,117
I’ll shout a magic word and set the world in place

506
00:38:00,117 --> 00:38:02,917
Whatever it may cost, there’s no reason to stop

507
00:38:02,917 --> 00:38:04,917
For a world that I cherish and love

508
00:38:04,917 --> 00:38:07,617
Monsters might be a scary foe to fight

509
00:38:07,617 --> 00:38:10,617
But I’ll take the stand if I can stop your tears and wipe them dry

510
00:38:10,617 --> 00:38:13,317
I’ll make you feel M@GICAL!

511
00:38:14,417 --> 00:38:19,517
If my pain's a type of cure for peace, I don’t mind. I can play as a nurse healing you everyday

512
00:38:19,517 --> 00:38:22,117
So what if I might shed a tear, get some bruises?

513
00:38:22,117 --> 00:38:25,117
A wipe is all I need to clean the cherry blush away, ha!

514
00:38:25,117 --> 00:38:27,817
Fighting through the night, but I’m wide awake

515
00:38:27,817 --> 00:38:30,117
It can all be so hard for me to get through the day

516
00:38:30,117 --> 00:38:32,917
Your smile is enough to heal all my aches

517
00:38:32,917 --> 00:38:34,317
Wrapped in a cute band-aid

518
00:38:34,317 --> 00:38:36,617
I can take the pain, fight all day

519
00:38:36,617 --> 00:38:37,917
Fill up the syringe with love

520
00:38:37,917 --> 00:38:40,117
Heal up the world and go again

521
00:38:40,117 --> 00:38:44,317
Super powerful Miku-chan!

522
00:38:44,317 --> 00:38:49,117
Miku Miku Miku go!

523
00:38:49,917 --> 00:38:54,917
And now, it's time for the moment you've been waiting for!

524
00:38:55,117 --> 00:38:58,617
1! 2! 3! Ready?!

525
00:38:59,117 --> 00:39:02,117
Miku Miku beam!

526
00:39:02,117 --> 00:39:08,617
Keep going!

527
00:39:09,117 --> 00:39:12,917
On my own, without anyone to know

528
00:39:12,917 --> 00:39:15,617
How my job’s not all rainbows

529
00:39:15,617 --> 00:39:19,617
But then I think about your smile... (Your words are so lyric☆l)

530
00:39:19,617 --> 00:39:22,617
I’m a magically bright invincible girl!

531
00:39:22,617 --> 00:39:24,917
If you need me to heal, go on and call out my name

532
00:39:24,917 --> 00:39:27,917
When you find yourself going down a spiral

533
00:39:27,917 --> 00:39:30,317
I’ll bonk away what puts you down, a pink hammer melee! Yah!

534
00:39:30,317 --> 00:39:32,917
Fighting through the night, but I’m wide awake

535
00:39:32,917 --> 00:39:35,417
All alone it’s so hard for me to get through the rain

536
00:39:35,417 --> 00:39:37,917
Your smile is enough to make my day

537
00:39:37,917 --> 00:39:40,317
So I stand tall and brave, ‘cause I’m not afraid

538
00:39:40,317 --> 00:39:42,617
Any pain I can laugh away

539
00:39:42,617 --> 00:39:44,917
Chin up, with love I’ll fight on till the end

540
00:40:04,892 --> 00:40:08,592
Bearing through the pain, I'll try to be brave

541
00:40:09,392 --> 00:40:13,292
As long as you can stay happy, I'm okay

542
00:40:13,592 --> 00:40:15,092
I'm not gonna bend, ha!

543
00:40:15,192 --> 00:40:19,192
I can be a cure for peace in your heart and I'll play as a nurse healing you everyday

544
00:40:19,292 --> 00:40:21,892
Your smile is enough to heal all my aches

545
00:40:22,092 --> 00:40:24,492
So in a cute band-aid

546
00:40:24,592 --> 00:40:27,292
If you're feeling pain, call my name, I'll be by your side

547
00:40:27,392 --> 00:40:29,892
Till I see your smile beam bright again

548
00:40:30,092 --> 00:40:34,692
Oya oya oya oya ooh! Fighter! Super powerful Miku-chan!

549
00:40:35,092 --> 00:40:39,592
Oya oya oya oya ooh! Cyber! Miku Miku Miku GO!

550
00:40:40,892 --> 00:40:43,092
あぁ、眠いよ〜
Ah, I'm so sleepy...

551
00:40:59,092 --> 00:41:00,092
あっ
Ah!

552
00:41:01,392 --> 00:41:04,092
夢...だった？
Was it... a dream?

553
00:42:51,892 --> 00:42:53,092
知った
I knew...

554
00:42:53,292 --> 00:42:56,292
救いのない形だった
It was a form beyond salvation,

555
00:42:56,592 --> 00:42:58,592
僕の声は
my voice was.

556
00:42:58,892 --> 00:43:00,092
知った
I knew...

557
00:43:00,292 --> 00:43:04,592
救いのない赤い血が流れているんだ
Irredeemable red blood flows within me.

558
00:43:05,192 --> 00:43:08,892
ただただ襲い来る影ばかり
Shadows that endlessly attack,

559
00:43:09,092 --> 00:43:12,492
揶揄う言葉 立ち上がれない夜風
mocking words, a night wind keeping me down.

560
00:43:12,792 --> 00:43:15,592
赫く光る場所へ 裸足で駆け出したら
When I ran barefoot toward the red shining place,

561
00:43:15,892 --> 00:43:18,592
ただただ膝を抱えている貴方がいた
you were there, simply holding your knees.

562
00:43:18,892 --> 00:43:20,092
だから
So...

563
00:43:20,192 --> 00:43:21,092
ENCOUNT!

564
00:43:21,192 --> 00:43:24,092
悲劇ぶった天国へ
Toward a heaven playing tragic.

565
00:43:25,892 --> 00:43:27,592
不甲斐ない瞳
Pathetic eyes,

566
00:43:27,692 --> 00:43:30,092
きっとあの日みつめた
that surely stared at those days,

567
00:43:30,292 --> 00:43:32,492
貴方のせいで
all because of you.

568
00:43:32,592 --> 00:43:38,892
はやく はやく...
Quickly, quickly...

569
00:43:38,992 --> 00:43:40,492
身を委ねて
Surrender yourself.

570
00:43:40,592 --> 00:43:44,292
淡い水面の向こうと
Beyond the faint surface of the water,

571
00:43:45,092 --> 00:43:47,092
視線
a gaze.

572
00:44:00,092 --> 00:44:01,292
知った
I knew...

573
00:44:01,492 --> 00:44:04,292
救いのない熱を持った
Possessing a heat beyond salvation,

574
00:44:04,492 --> 00:44:06,892
僕の炎波
my flame wave.

575
00:44:07,092 --> 00:44:08,292
歌った
I sang...

576
00:44:08,492 --> 00:44:12,592
憂いのない貴方の眼は醜かった
Your sorrowless eyes were hideous,

577
00:44:12,892 --> 00:44:28,092
酷く
so cruelly...

578
00:44:41,892 --> 00:44:52,092
呆然としているその顔に触れてみたかった
I wanted to touch that stunned face of yours.

579
00:44:54,092 --> 00:44:55,292
だから
So...

580
00:44:55,392 --> 00:44:56,292
ENCOUNT!

581
00:44:56,392 --> 00:44:59,892
喜劇ぶった天国へ
Toward a heaven playing comedic.

582
00:45:02,440 --> 00:45:04,040
奪い合う瞳
Eyes claiming each other,

583
00:45:04,040 --> 00:45:05,840
屹度 あの日
surely, that day

584
00:45:05,840 --> 00:45:07,140
崩れた
that collapsed,

585
00:45:07,140 --> 00:45:08,940
貴方のせいだ
it was all because of you.

586
00:45:08,940 --> 00:45:13,940
はやく はやく はやく...
Faster, faster, faster...

587
00:45:13,940 --> 00:45:15,340
ねえ 教えて
Hey, tell me.

588
00:45:15,340 --> 00:45:20,640
深海 樹海 秘密のむこうへと
Deep sea, sea of trees, to the other side of secrets.

589
00:45:30,140 --> 00:45:31,840
不甲斐ない瞳
Pathetic eyes,

590
00:45:31,840 --> 00:45:33,640
屹度 あの日
surely, that day

591
00:45:33,640 --> 00:45:34,940
偽った
lied,

592
00:45:34,940 --> 00:45:36,640
君のせいだ
it was all because of you.

593
00:45:36,640 --> 00:45:42,640
はやく はやく はやく...
Faster, faster, faster...

594
00:45:42,640 --> 00:45:48,140
息を止めて 泡や泡になり むこうへと
Hold your breath, turn into bubbles and foam, to the other side.

595
00:45:50,640 --> 00:45:53,440
白い光をみつめていると
When I stare at the white light,

596
00:45:53,440 --> 00:45:56,940
急な痛みに襲われる
a sudden pain attacks me.

597
00:45:56,940 --> 00:46:01,140
僕が私を保っていられなくなること
That I can no longer maintain myself,

598
00:46:01,140 --> 00:46:06,640
それをこの小さな器が証明している
this small vessel proves it.

599
00:46:06,640 --> 00:46:11,140
初めに 安堵する君がみたい
First, I want to see you relieved.

600
00:46:11,140 --> 00:46:16,140
次に 期待したい
Next, I want to have expectations.

601
00:46:33,640 --> 00:46:37,140
この場所で戦いなど起こっていない。
There was no major battle here.

602
00:46:37,940 --> 00:46:41,340
少なくこともこの世界線では...
At least not in this timeline...

603
00:46:42,640 --> 00:46:50,640
だが探偵には分かっていた。彼女が見たものは決して夢ではないことを。
But the detective knows what she saw was no dream.

604
00:46:51,640 --> 00:46:56,640
心の中にはまだ殺戮の匂いが漂っている。
The smell of the carnage still lingers in her mind.

605
00:46:57,640 --> 00:47:04,140
かつての彼女にまとわりついていた、あの匂い。
It's a scent that was, at one time, so familiar to her.

606
00:47:04,640 --> 00:47:15,640
探偵としての生活も今では順調だが、そうでなければあの匂いからは離れることができなかったでしょう。
That stench would still linger on her if the detective's life didn't take a turn for the better.

607
00:47:16,340 --> 00:47:22,640
今でも...あの頃の日々がリアルな夢のようにまとわりつく。
Even now... her days felt more like the real dream.

608
00:47:23,640 --> 00:47:27,140
終わるべくして終わったおとぎ話。
A fairytale. Maybe one that deserved to end.

609
00:47:27,340 --> 00:47:35,640
どこまで行っても彼女は、生まれ持った本質から逃れることはできない。
Because, at the end of the day, she can never run away from her nature.

610
00:47:39,640 --> 00:47:44,640
それでも今は違う。今の彼女には仲間がいる。
But she's not just that anymore. She has friends to thank for that.

611
00:47:45,140 --> 00:47:51,140
それが、別の世界線の彼女とは違う点なのかもしれない。
Maybe that was what separated her from the other version.

612
00:47:52,640 --> 00:48:00,640
もしかしたらあの子は、幸せに生きることのできた世界線があったのだろうかと、
And, maybe... that version of herself just wanted a ray of hope,

613
00:48:01,140 --> 00:48:06,140
そんな一筋の希望を求めていたのだろうか。
to know that there was one timeline where things worked out.

614
00:48:06,940 --> 00:48:16,640
そしてその幸せな世界線というのは、ここではないまた別の世界線のことかもしれない...
Or perhaps this was never about the detective...

615
00:48:17,140 --> 00:48:23,140
考えが頭を巡るものの、答えが出ることはない。
so many thoughts run amak inside her head, but they're forever left unanswered.

616
00:48:24,140 --> 00:48:32,140
何にせよ、探偵は自身の血塗られた過去を忘れることはないでしょう。
Whatever the case, the detective won't forget her bloody past, but she isn't going to revert to it either.

617
00:48:32,940 --> 00:48:42,640
しかしまた後戻りするつもりもない。彼女はこれからも仲間とともに進む。
She will continue to move forward with her friends,

618
00:48:43,640 --> 00:48:50,140
望んだ結末を迎えられなかった別の自分たちのためにも。
and for all the variants who didn't get their desired ending.

619
00:48:50,640 --> 00:48:54,140
探偵アーニャ・メルフィッサは、
The detective, Anya Melfissa,

620
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:58,940
明日に向かって生き続ける。
will keep on living for her own tomorrow.

621
00:49:09,140 --> 00:49:16,340
Anya Melfissa Birthday Live 2024!

622
00:49:16,640 --> 00:49:18,940
How did everyone like it?!

623
00:49:19,140 --> 00:49:20,640
Oh, my goodness!

624
00:49:20,640 --> 00:49:25,140
やっと今年も参りました、アーニャの誕生日です！
It's finally here again this year, it's Anya's birthday!

625
00:49:25,140 --> 00:49:27,140
いかがでしたでしょうか？
How was it?

626
00:49:27,340 --> 00:49:33,140
This time, I tried to incorporate a little bit of story into my 3D birthday celebration,

627
00:49:33,140 --> 00:49:37,140
and I think it turned out pretty nice, you know?

628
00:49:37,140 --> 00:49:41,140
You get story part, and also live part,

629
00:49:41,140 --> 00:49:44,340
and I think it turned out pretty well!

630
00:49:44,340 --> 00:49:48,140
And also, how was my new original song? Oh, my goodness!

631
00:49:48,140 --> 00:49:52,140
How was my new original song? It was good, wasn't it?

632
00:49:52,140 --> 00:49:54,940
I hope you all liked it.

633
00:49:54,940 --> 00:49:58,340
新曲もね、あの、歌わせていただきました。いかがでしたでしょうか？
I was able to perform my new song too. How did you like it?

634
00:50:00,115 --> 00:50:01,415
Ah! Oh my god!

635
00:50:01,415 --> 00:50:08,315
I celebrated my birthday with a lot of friends too this year.

636
00:50:08,315 --> 00:50:12,815
Yeah, a lot of the girls came to celebrate my birthday,

637
00:50:12,815 --> 00:50:17,415
and also Detective Anya managed to solve that mission.

638
00:50:17,415 --> 00:50:21,015
Wow, she's got it! Detective Anya.

639
00:50:21,015 --> 00:50:23,815
Did you guys like Detective Anya as well?

640
00:50:23,815 --> 00:50:27,315
Detective Anya was pretty cool, but not as cool as me!

641
00:50:27,315 --> 00:50:30,915
Oh my god, and also special guests!

642
00:50:30,915 --> 00:50:33,915
There were special guests!

643
00:50:33,915 --> 00:50:40,115
Oh my god, I can't believe I got to sing with Hatsune Miku! Hatsune Miku-chan!

644
00:50:40,115 --> 00:50:44,015
Oh my god, she was really cute!

645
00:50:44,015 --> 00:50:48,915
And also for the narration for my story part, Ueda Reina-san narrated it!

646
00:50:48,915 --> 00:50:58,815
Oh my god! 上田麗奈さんがやってくれました！
Oh my god! Reina Ueda-san did the narration!

647
00:50:58,815 --> 00:51:06,715
ありがとうございます！ミクちゃんとも歌ったし、いや盛りだくさんでしたねー、今年。
Thank you so much! I sang with Miku-chan too, it was packed full of stuff this year!

648
00:51:06,715 --> 00:51:14,415
Oh my god, lots of wild things happening on this year's birthday live! How did you guys like it?

649
00:51:14,415 --> 00:51:18,615
How did you guys like it? Oh my gosh!

650
00:51:18,615 --> 00:51:23,715
Yeah, I had a lot of fun! But...

651
00:51:23,715 --> 00:51:28,915
I would like to make an announcement this year. It's the usual!

652
00:51:28,915 --> 00:51:31,815
ここで告知があります！
We have an announcement here!

653
00:51:31,815 --> 00:51:35,415
I have an announcement to make! Let me make an announcement!

654
00:51:35,415 --> 00:51:37,415
はい！こちら！
Yes! Here it is!

655
00:51:37,415 --> 00:51:47,915
Oh my god, what is that? Who is that? Is that me? Yes, it is! We're releasing some new merchandise this year!

656
00:51:47,915 --> 00:51:51,715
What do we have? Let's take a look at them, shall we?

657
00:51:51,715 --> 00:51:57,215
そして、えーっと、1つずつ見ていきましょう！まずは、こちらです！
And, um, let's take a look at them one by one! First is this one!

658
00:51:57,215 --> 00:52:03,315
It's a canvas art! "Study Time with Anya!" Canvas art!

659
00:52:03,315 --> 00:52:08,915
Oh my god, this illustration is so cute! It's illustrated by Lunar-sensei!

660
00:52:08,915 --> 00:52:14,015
Lunar先生に、イラストを描いていただきました！可愛い！
Lunar-sensei drew this illustration for me! Cute!

661
00:52:14,015 --> 00:52:22,915
The theme is, you know, literary girl. Oh my god, so smart, so intelligent!

662
00:52:22,915 --> 00:52:27,515
文学少女というテーマになっております！
It has the theme of a literary girl!

663
00:52:27,515 --> 00:52:29,115
次はこちら！
Next is this!

664
00:52:29,115 --> 00:52:33,315
"Study Time with Anya!" The notebook!

665
00:52:33,315 --> 00:52:39,115
I think this is my first notebook! I've never had a notebook as merchandise before! Oh my goodness!

666
00:52:39,115 --> 00:52:44,315
Please use this lots for all your notes, for anything!

667
00:52:44,315 --> 00:52:49,015
色々メモしてね！オリジナルノートでございます！
Take lots of notes! It's an original notebook!

668
00:52:49,015 --> 00:52:50,615
と、次はこちら！
And next is this!

669
00:52:50,615 --> 00:52:56,115
It's a pen case! How cute is that! ペンポーチです！
It's a pen case! How cute is that! It's a pen pouch!

670
00:52:56,115 --> 00:53:05,215
ペンポーチも初かな？ ノートも初らしい、ペンポーチもなんと、初です！
Is a pen pouch a first too? The notebook is a first, and the pen pouch is also a first!

671
00:53:05,215 --> 00:53:09,715
ぜひ一緒にね、あのノートと使ってください！
Please use it together with the notebook!

672
00:53:09,715 --> 00:53:18,615
Use this along with the note, I think they would go really well together, okay?

673
00:53:18,615 --> 00:53:20,915
次はこちら！
Next is this!

674
00:53:20,915 --> 00:53:28,815
今年もボイスが出ます！そして今年もえー、アーニャが台本を書かせていただいております！
There's a voice pack again this year! And Anya wrote the script again this year!

675
00:53:28,815 --> 00:53:41,315
I wrote the script as usual, as usual for every year! I wrote the script for this situational voice, so please get it! Please get it!

676
00:53:41,315 --> 00:53:47,415
Oh yeah, the voice will be in Japanese, but there will be scripts in Indonesian, English, and Japanese!

677
00:53:47,415 --> 00:53:52,415
ちなみにボイス自体は日本語になりますけど...
By the way, the voice audio itself is in Japanese, but...

678
00:53:52,415 --> 00:53:59,915
えっと、台本もついて...ついてきます！インドネシア語と英語と日本語の台本があります！
um, scripts are... scripts are included! Scripts in Indonesian, English, and Japanese are included!

679
00:53:59,915 --> 00:54:03,215
ぜひ聴いてください！
Please listen to it!

680
00:54:03,215 --> 00:54:06,115
そしてフルセット購入特典はこちら！
And here is the full set purchase bonus!

681
00:54:06,115 --> 00:54:23,715
Oh my god! Limited Edition Birthday Set has... what is that? A hand-signed autograph?! Oh my god, it's the first for me! Anya's first-ever hand-signed autograph for Limited Edition! Please get them!

682
00:54:23,715 --> 00:54:26,615
なんと、今年はサイン入りです！
It comes with a signature this year!

683
00:54:26,615 --> 00:54:41,215
今年はサイン入りです！なんと、なんと、なんと！初、初ですね！アーニャが自らサインをして... 初なので、ぜひ皆さんこの機会でゲットしてください！
It comes with a signature this year! Wow, wow, wow! It's the first time Anya is personally signing them... Since it's a first, please take this chance to get it!

684
00:54:41,215 --> 00:54:55,815
Yeah, please get the Limited Edition! And for the Standard Edition, it includes a foil-stamped replica autograph, so don't worry if you miss out on the Limited Edition! Yeah!

685
00:54:55,815 --> 00:55:00,115
ということでグッズ紹介は以上です！That's all for the merch!
So that's all for the merchandise intro! That's all for the merch!

686
00:55:00,163 --> 00:55:01,463
Introduction!

687
00:55:01,463 --> 00:55:07,663
And another announcement is that my original song, the one that you guys heard...

688
00:55:07,663 --> 00:55:10,663
...it's called ENCA or ENCOUNT, by the way.

689
00:55:10,663 --> 00:55:17,663
It will be releasing digitally in like a few hours!

690
